<header><h1>The L1Z1X Mindnet: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_lizix">The L1Z1X Mindnet</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="assimilate"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Assimilate">Assimilate</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Any space docks that are placed by this ability during a tactical action may produce units during the <b>Production</b> step of that tactical action.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I produce at my home space dock during a tactical action elsewhere &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the production step only uses units in the system you just activated.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the L1Z1X player resolves their <sc>Assimilate</sc> ability, and then plays the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Infiltrate"><i>Infiltrate</i></a> action card, or vice versa, they will replace zero PDS and space docks with zero PDS and space docks when they resolve the latter ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the L1Z1X player would have to place a structure, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may, but are not required to, remove a structure of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead.<sup>1,2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 23.4a: &ldquo;that player can remove a unit from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any instance of &lsquo;replace&rsquo; can be considered to say &lsquo;remove and place&rsquo; if no units are left in reinforcements, and would be covered by Component Limitations in the LRR.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If my reinforcements are empty, must I take units from the board to place a new one?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; the rules let you remove a unit from the board to place it elsewhere, but you are not required to. This matters for effects such as L1Z1X Assimilate or Swords to Plowshares.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If all my space docks or PDS are on the board, can I place another?&rdquo;: &ldquo;if none are in reinforcements, you may take one from a system without your command token and place it where the effect directs.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the L1Z1X player gains control of a planet, they also replace coexisting structures on that planet.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Do the L1Z1X replace coexisting structures when they gain control of a planet? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="harrow"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow">Harrow</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <a href="/R_planetary_shield"><sc>Planetary Shield</sc></a> ability will prevent the use of the <sc>Harrow</sc> ability on a planet.<sup>1,2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 65.2: &ldquo;The &lsquo;Planetary Shield&rsquo; ability prevents an L1Z1X player from using their &lsquo;Harrow&rsquo; faction ability.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the L1Z1X Harrow ability work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Planetary Shield stops it.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play, Planetary Shield: the planet &ldquo;is not an eligible target&rdquo; for Bombardment.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The L1Z1X player cannot use their <sc>Harrow</sc> ability if they are not the active player.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the L1Z1X use harrow when they&rsquo;re defending during ground combat? A: No, only the active player can use BOMBARDMENT.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The L1Z1X player may use their <sc>Harrow</sc> ability at the end of the round in which their last ground force was destroyed. This may cause the combat to end in a draw.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the L1Z1X Harrow ability work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It still resolves after the round in which L1Z1X lose their last ground force; if it then kills the last defender, the combat is a draw.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The combat ending doesn&rsquo;t nullify the end of a round of combat trigger. Harrow, in this case, would still resolve.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Every unit in the active system with the <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> ability may use it against the planet the ground combat is taking place on, regardless of whether that unit bombarded that planet during the <b>Bombardment</b> step of the invasion.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the L1Z1X Harrow ability work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Every ship with Bombardment there can join in, not just those that bombarded that planet.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Dane, Feb 16, 2018), &ldquo;&hellip;can they use EVERY ship in the system, or only those that originally bombarded the planet before the combat?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Each ship in the system can be part of Harrow.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR errata: &ldquo;The text of the L1Z1X&rsquo;s &lsquo;Harrow&rsquo; faction ability should read as follows: &lsquo;At the end of each round of ground combat, your ships in the active system may use their bombardment abilities against your opponent&rsquo;s ground forces on the planet.&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>An Annihilator may bombard when using <sc>Harrow</sc> if that mech is not currently participating in ground combat, even if it has been committed to a different planet, and has been or will be involved in another ground combat during the current invasion.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can L1Z1X mechs bombard through Harrow?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Only when not in that ground combat: a mech fighting on a planet can&rsquo;t bombard it, but one on another planet in the system can.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The L1Z1X player may use the ability of the <span class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#X-89_Bacterial_Weapon"><i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;</i></a></span> or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#X-89_Bacterial_Weapon"><i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;&Omega;</i></a> technologies whenever they bombard.<sup>10,15</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Are there common clarifications for specific objectives &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Harrow is Bombardment.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>10</sup> Codex I, X-89 Bacterial Weapon: &ldquo;After 1 or more of your units use BOMBARDMENT against a planet, if at least 1 of your opponent&rsquo;s infantry was destroyed, you may destroy all of your opponent&rsquo;s infantry on that planet.&rdquo; triggers whenever units use BOMBARDMENT.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>15</sup> Codex 4.5 Technology Card Updates, X-89 Bacterial Weapon: &ldquo;Double the hits produced by your units&rsquo; BOMBARDMENT and ground combat rolls.&rdquo; applies to any BOMBARDMENT use.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="cybernetic-enhancements" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Cybernetic%20Enhancements">Cybernetic Enhancements</a> (replaced by &Omega;) <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega; version.<sup>10</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>10</sup> Codex I p. 8, &ldquo;The Omega Initiative&rdquo;: &ldquo;Components from this section replace preexisting components of the same name and type.&rdquo; The Omega Initiative contents (p. 3) list &ldquo;Cybernetic Enhancements&rdquo;.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the L1Z1X player has no command tokens in their strategy pool, <i>Cybernetic Enhancements</i> cannot be played.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can L1Z1X Cybernetic Enhancements or Xxcha Political Favor be used if their owner has no command token in the strategy pool?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; &hellip; if there is no token to remove, nothing on it resolves.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The command tokens must be present in order to resolve these PNs.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="cybernetic-enhancements-omega"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Cybernetic%20Enhancements">Cybernetic Enhancements &Omega;</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
