<h2 id="i48s"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=I48S">I48S</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The infantry must be in the system when it is activated for it to be eligible to be replaced. It cannot be replaced if it is moved into or produced in the active system later in the turn.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a mech, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a mech from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The mech will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 23.4a: &ldquo;that player can remove a unit from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="2ram"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=2RAM">2RAM</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Those units still have <a href="/R_planetary_shield"><sc>Planetary Shield</sc></a>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. LRR 65.3a covers war suns: &ldquo;Units treated as if they do not have a &lsquo;Planetary Shield&rsquo; ability cannot use the &lsquo;Magen Defense Grid&rsquo;&rdquo; technology.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li class="removed">The player that owns those units may still use the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Magen_Defense_Grid"><i>Magen Defense Grid</i></a> technology.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. LRR 65.3a covers war suns: &ldquo;Units treated as if they do not have a &lsquo;Planetary Shield&rsquo; ability cannot use the &lsquo;Magen Defense Grid&rsquo;&rdquo; technology.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-helmsman"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=The%20Helmsman">The Helmsman</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=Dark%20Space%20Navigation">Dark Space Navigation</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Ships in systems with one of the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s command tokens may move.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do the Argent and L1Z1X heroes move ships &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;ignoring command tokens in the systems they leave.&rdquo; (Stated for the Argent hero.)</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s ships move outside of a tactical action, they may transport units from systems that contain the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s command tokens.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The LRR will be updated to reflect that transportation of units out of systems that contain your command tokens are only applicable during tactical actions. During Movement abilities, you can transport units out of systems that contain your tokens.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships move directly to their destination system. They may only transport units from their origin system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do the Argent and L1Z1X heroes move ships &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;no path or move value &hellip; The ships can carry units starting with them, but can&rsquo;t pick up along a path.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships moving out of a gravity rift must roll for removal.<sup>1,2,3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do gravity rifts work &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Each ship that leaves or passes through a rift rolls, and is removed on a 1-3.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;A ship that moves through or out of a gravity rift applies +1 to its move value and then rolls one die.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Do ships roll when moving out of a gravity rift due to the Mahact Hero, Benediction? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR quick reference: &ldquo;Each Ship Moving Through or Out of Applies +1 Move and Rolls 1 die.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Ships do not roll for removal if the L1Z1X player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Codex_IV:~:text=Circlet%20of%20the%20Void"><i>Circlet of the Void</i></a> relic.<sup>11</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>11</sup> Codex IV, Circlet of the Void: &ldquo;Your units do not roll for gravity rifts, and you ignore the movement effects of other anomalies.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Ships cannot move into a supernova, even with <i>Dark Space Navigation</i>.<sup>1,2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When an ability moves units outside a tactical action &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Anomaly rules still apply, so no ability moves ships into a supernova unless it says so.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;A ship cannot move through or into a supernova.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 86.1: &ldquo;A ship cannot move through or into a supernova.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Ships may move into a supernova if the L1Z1X player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Codex_IV:~:text=Circlet%20of%20the%20Void"><i>Circlet of the Void</i></a> relic.<sup>11</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>11</sup> Codex IV, Circlet of the Void: &ldquo;Your units do not roll for gravity rifts, and you ignore the movement effects of other anomalies.&rdquo; That includes the supernova&rsquo;s restriction on moving into it.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Ships may travel into an asteroid field only if the L1Z1X player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Antimass_Deflectors"><i>Antimass Deflectors</i></a> technology.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;Anomaly rules still apply.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li><i>Dark Space Navigation</i> may be used to move ships into the wormhole nexus. If the nexus is inactive, this will cause it to activate.<sup>1,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 100.1: &ldquo;The wormhole nexus begins the game in play with its inactive side up.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook describes the two sides of the Wormhole Nexus.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="annihilator"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Mech:~:text=Annihilator">Annihilator</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>An Annihilator may bombard when using the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow"><sc>Harrow</sc></a> ability if that mech is not currently participating in ground combat, even if it has been committed to a different planet, and has been or will be involved in another ground combat during the current invasion.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can L1Z1X mechs bombard through Harrow?&rdquo;: &ldquo;a mech fighting on a planet can&rsquo;t bombard it, but one on another planet in the system can.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

